<title>RUSSIA: Russia to offer 12 trln rbls in T-bills Feb 26.</title>
<headline>Russia to offer 12 trln rbls in T-bills Feb 26.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will offer 7.50 trillion roubles in 357-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 23002) and 4.50 trillion roubles in 91-day T-bills (series 21072) on February 26, the Central Bank said on Wednesday. Full details of the auctions follow:  </p>
<p>Full details of the 357-day auction:</p>
<p>    Series number	     23002</p>
<p>    Issue volume		7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations	     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date		  Feb 26, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor			 357 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date	     Feb 18, 1998</p>
<p>Full details of the 91-day auction:</p>
<p>    Series number	     21072</p>
<p>    Issue date		  4.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations	     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date		  Feb 26, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor			 91 day</p>
<p>    Maturity date	     May 28, 1997</p>
<p>On February 26 the Finance Ministry will also pay about 687.12 billion roubles in interest on OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24006) and about 329.48 billion roubles in interest on OFZ bonds (series 24004).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
